00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:28.790
Park-jya-song?

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:29.856
- Pok-Jay-Song.

00:00:29.856 --> 00:00:31.064
It sounded right to me.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.587
- [Voiceover] Ok Taec-Yeon.

00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:33.400
- Okay?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.863
It's not okay, though.

00:00:34.863 --> 00:00:35.716
Oh?

00:00:35.716 --> 00:00:36.651
Um, one of these letters is solid.

00:00:36.651 --> 00:00:37.849
- O-Kay-Taw-Kyoon.

00:00:37.849 --> 00:00:39.936
- Oh-Kay Tayk-Yone.

00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:41.025
Oh Take-On?

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.440
- Awk-Ty-Awk.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.552
I can't get my head straight.

00:00:44.552 --> 00:00:46.623
- A lot of times my mind will
translate it to English for me

00:00:46.623 --> 00:00:48.874
so it'd be like oh tech young,

00:00:48.874 --> 00:00:50.621
And that's like, probably not the way

00:00:50.621 --> 00:00:51.739
